        "source_locator": null,
        "speaker_label": "விங்கன்",
        "speaker_label_origin": "source-explicit",
        "source_delimiter": ":—",
        "page_provenance": [
          {
            "pdf_page": 85,
            "printed_page": 84
          }
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "english_text": "When I said, ‘The illusion will lift and the people will know the truth,’ you mocked me: ‘An attempt to twist sand into rope!’ Now I have come after twisting a rope out of sand! Not an empty rope—a hanging rope fit for you! When I said I would tear away your disguise, you jeered, ‘Will you bend the sky into a bow?’ Now I have come not to bend the sky, but to bend your honour itself! You warned me, ‘Don't play the snake-charmer's pipe while standing on a volcano!’ I have already smashed that ‘volcano man,’ bone from sinew, and come here!...",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": []
      }
    },
