          {
            "pdf_page": 86,
            "printed_page": 85
          }
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "english_text": "I didn't go mad today! That day in my childhood, when in a children's game I tied the thaali around your daughter's neck and you beat me—that very day I went mad! You shoved aside my mother when she stopped you from beating me, the mother who embraced and protected me with care, and tore open the body of the woman who gave birth to me.... Sinner! Blood gushed from the womb in which I had lived; if the vow I took then, with that blood as witness, is called madness!... Until that madness is quenched, I have no other work! No other work!....",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "This cross-page source speech contains compressed/irregular wording around the mother-protection action. English preserves the evident source action without changing the closed Tamil record."
        ]
      }
    },
